"""A program holds its declared inputs and nothing the source tree has beside them.

Bazel stages every input as a symlink into the source tree. tsgo reads a root
file at its staged path and resolves a type reference directive to its realpath,
that file's own imports from there; a path-shaped `types` entry is a root file
of the action tsconfig, not a directive. `bindings.d.ts` names `./stray` in a
`typeof import()`, and `stray.ts` is checked in beside it, in no target's srcs,
holding a type error. Read at the staged path the import resolves to nothing
and `skipLibCheck` drops the TS2307 inside the .d.ts; read at the realpath it
resolves to the source-tree file, and the build fails on an error in a file the
target never named.
"""

# stray.ts is the fixture, the one file that must be in no target's srcs.
# gazelle:exclude stray.ts

# Compiler options, not data: named by the tsconfig attr.
# gazelle:exclude tsconfig.bindings.json

load("@bazel_skylib//rules:build_test.bzl", "build_test")
load("//ts:defs.bzl", "ts_compile")

package(default_visibility = ["//:__pkg__"])

ts_compile(
    name = "bindings",
    srcs = ["bindings.d.ts"],
)

# The shape the monorepo trial failed in: a wrangler-generated
# worker-configuration.d.ts reached through `types`, holding `typeof import("./src/index")`.
ts_compile(
    name = "app",
    srcs = ["app.ts"],
    tsconfig = "tsconfig.bindings.json",
    deps = [":bindings"],
)

build_test(
    name = "app_test",
    targets = [":app"],
)
